'''viverrine''' (vī-ver′in), ''a.'' and ''n.'' [< NL. ''viverrinus'', < L. ''viverra'', a ferret: see ''viverra''.] '''I.''' ''a.'' Of or pertaining to the ''Viverridæ;'' viverriform in a proper sense; more particularly, belonging to the ''Viverrinæ;'' not herpestine.—{{smaller|'''Viverrine cat''', the wagati, ''Felis viverrina'' of India, a true cat.—'''Viverrine dasyure''', a variety of ''Dasyurus maugei'' of South Australia and Tasmania.}}

'''II.''' ''n.'' A member of the ''Viverridæ'', and especially of the ''Viverrinæ''.

Also ''viverrin''.
